virglrenderer: Venus binds an app's image to a swapchain's memory on both drivers

What: overrides the KosmicKrisp-only exception in virgl-venus-dedicated-memory.patch's
header. An ALIAS_BIT image with the create info of the ALIAS_BIT image a memory is
dedicated to may bind to that memory at offset 0 on MoltenVK too. That is what guest Mesa
sends for an app's image bound with VkBindImageMemorySwapchainInfoKHR: it makes the image
from the swapchain's create info and binds it to the swapchain image's dedicated memory.
Such an image holds the memory for every bind vkr passes on, whatever the driver returns.
A memory the guest frees then stays in the driver as a zombie until the image's driver
destroy, also a deferred one (the image is itself a dedicated target). The order is: the
image, the memory, the image the memory was dedicated to. Refused with a log line: an
ALIAS_BIT image with other create info (type, format, tiling, flags, usage, extent,
levels, layers, samples), a second bind of such an image, and one image twice in one
vkBindImageMemory2. KosmicKrisp let those through before. All memory frees (vkFreeMemory,
the device's teardown, a zombie's last holder) go through one helper,
vkr_device_memory_free.
Why: MoltenVK 1.4.2 binds an aliasable image to dedicated memory (MVKDeviceMemory.mm:171)
but counts it only in non-dedicated memory (:175). So ~MVKDeviceMemory never clears the
image's pointer to the memory, and vkDestroyImage later locks the freed memory's mutex
(removeImageMemoryBinding). Freeing the swapchain's memory before the app's image is legal
(vkDestroySwapchainKHR has only VUIDs 01282-01284). Driver probe on the M1 Max: every run
that freed the memory first crashed on MoltenVK (60 SIGABRT, 60 SIGSEGV under libgmalloc),
none on KosmicKrisp. The image draws from the target's MTLTexture (MVKImage.mm:105-111),
so it must match the target. vkr refused the bind on MoltenVK before, which ended the
app's context.
Upstream: OmacVM policy (VUIDs VkImageSwapchainCreateInfoKHR-swapchain-00995,
VkBindImageMemoryInfo-image-07460, vkBindImageMemory2-pBindInfos-04006,
vkBindImageMemory-memory-02628); nothing posted to MoltenVK.
Tests: Tests/virgl/test-venus-commands.c (the x-dedicated-alias cases, also under
libgmalloc).

